    "problemStatement": "We define f(A)f(A)f(A) as the minimum positive integer XXX such that the following condition holds:\n\n\nFor each iii (1≤i≤∣A∣1 \\le i \\le |A|1≤i≤∣A∣), there exists j≠ij \\ne ij=i (1≤j≤∣A∣1 \\le j \\le |A|1≤j≤∣A∣), such that ∣Ai−Aj∣≤X|A_i - A_j| \\le X∣Ai​−Aj​∣≤X.\nFor arrays of size 111, i.e. ∣A∣=1|A| = 1∣A∣=1, we define f(A)=0f(A) = 0f(A)=0. For other arrays, it can be proven there exists at least one such integer.\n\nYou are given an integer NNN. Let B=[1,2,3,…,N]B = [1, 2, 3, \\ldots, N]B=[1,2,3,…,N].\n\nConsider the 2N−12^N - 12N−1 non-empty subsequences CCC of the array BBB possible, find the sum of f(C)f(C)f(C) over all such CCC.\n\nSince the answer may be large, print it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line contains a single integer NNN.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the sum of f(C)f(C)f(C) over all subsequences of [1,2,…,N][1, 2, \\ldots, N][1,2,…,N].",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤201 \\le T \\le 201≤T≤20",
      "2≤N≤20002 \\le N \\le 20002≤N≤2000"
    ],
